These optional examples are sourced as trusted shell code. Copy ONE example to
vee-custom.sh in your blog directory, then select its format with -f.

vee-custom-3rd-party.sh: -f par72, -f pandoc, or -f markdown. Install the selected
external program yourself. HTML uses that program; Gopher output stays literal.

vee-custom-utf8.sh: -f null (literal text) or -f groff-utf8. The UTF-8 formatter
uses groff-utf8 if available, otherwise groff with -Tutf8.

Custom formatters receive _OUTPUT_TYPE (html/gopher), RAW/gRAW, and FINAL/gFINAL.
Write to the supplied output path; vee stages it before replacing the published
file. Return a nonzero status on failure. Formatters see the complete raw post,
including its historical metadata header. Convert or strip it deliberately if
your chosen markup processor requires body-only input.
